note bw_yardsign Bonded yard notice | HARBOR AUTHORITY - BONDED YARD\nSeized goods, held pending sale.\n\nThe yard is laid out as a maze on purpose, by order of the Council, so that thieves lose themselves in it and are found in the morning, weighed, and fined.\n\nClerks carry the yard plan. Clerks do not lend the yard plan.\n\nTrespassers will be weighed.\n\n(Scratched into the paint underneath, small and neat: I hang a lamp at the turns I trust. Not at all of them. Nobody gets everything for free in this city - N.)
note bw_strongbox Seized goods strongbox | The seized-goods strongbox, its lid up: whatever the Authority took off the last boats in.
loot bw_strongbox CopperIngot*2;Bolt*3;TradeToken*2
prop bw_strongbox loot.refill=0
note bw_clerknote Clerk's last shift | Six years I was night clerk in this yard, and tonight is my last shift. Tomorrow they send me up to the Crown, to count water instead of crates.\n\nI am leaving the strongbox open. Everything in it was taken off people who were only trying to keep their children's water clean. Filters, mostly. Filters, and one tin tram with a clockwork key - the little six-forty, painted blue - which I gave back to the girl it belonged to. I would do it again.\n\nCouncillor Crane came to the yard once. He did not look at the crates. He stood with his hand flat on the concrete and listened to it, the way a doctor listens to a chest. Then he asked me what the yard weighed. All of it. I said I didn't know. He wrote a number down anyway, and underlined it twice.\n\n- Nell Abernethy, night clerk

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Breakwater Customs
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The edge of Highwater, the city on the drowned towers: a breakwater out to a customs house on a tower's top storey, a boom across the channel and the Harbor Authority's watch tower. The first island of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||A breakwater runs out to a building standing in the sea - the top floor of a tower, the rest of it drowned. Beyond it, on the horizon, more towers. The rumour is true.

story weighed|Cargo weighed|Note_Paper|Your cargo, weighed and chalked on the Authority's board.
story permit|Trader's permit|Note_Paper|A Harbor Authority trader's permit, stamped. Highwater's markets are open to you.

prop concrete tint.color=#9a9a94
prop concrete tint.amount=0.35
prop skyline tint.color=#7a8088
prop skyline tint.amount=0.4

prop weighscale obj.name=weighscale
prop weighscale beh.use=Weigh your cargo
prop weighscale if.use=!signal|weighed
prop weighscale on.use=signal||weighed\ngive||story:weighed*1\nmessage||The beam tips and settles. A clerk's hand has chalked the numbers on the board for years; you chalk your own.
prop weighscale else.use=message||Your cargo is weighed already.
prop permitstamp obj.name=permitstamp
prop permitstamp beh.use=Stamp a trader's permit
prop permitstamp if.use=signal|weighed\n!signal|permit
prop permitstamp on.use=signal||permit\ngive||story:permit*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||THUMP. HARBOR AUTHORITY - TRADER - ADMITTED. Under the stamp, the last line in the clerks' ledger: NIGHT CLERK N. ABERNETHY - REASSIGNED TO THE CROWN.
prop permitstamp else.use=message||No permit without a weighed cargo - the rules say so. Or you have one already.

note entryrules Authority entry rules | HARBOR AUTHORITY - ENTRY RULES\n\n1. Every vessel is weighed. Every cargo is chalked.\n2. Every trader carries a stamped permit.\n3. Water is the Authority's. Filters are the Authority's.\n4. The boom opens at dawn and closes at dusk.\n5. No one sails past Pumpcrown.\n\nThese rules are not cruelty. They are arithmetic. A city standing on drowned towers can carry so many people, so much cargo, so much want - and not one pound more. I have done the sums. Somebody has to.\n\nWelcome to Highwater. Keep to the rules and the city keeps you dry.\n\n- Councillor Aldous Crane, for the Harbor Council
note weighsign Weigh station | WEIGH STATION\n\nAll cargo on the scale. All numbers on the board.\nThen the permit desk.
note towersign Watch tower | AUTHORITY WATCH TOWER\nNo entry. The aerial is for official traffic.\n\n(The door is not locked. The guard left for the city a long time ago.)
note smugglertip A friend's tip | Folded small, in a hurry, tucked under the strongbox lid -\n\nYou got through Nell's yard. Good. Then you can get through a city.\n\nForget the Authority's prices. The bazaar sells what the Authority says doesn't exist: filters, real ones, the kind the Council says nobody makes any more. Raft Row, on band six hundred. Look for the pedlar with the green awning, and don't tell him your permit number.\n\nI can't give you my name yet. Somebody in this city reads every letter that comes past the breakwater, and I would like to go on breathing. I'll leave you notes where I can.\n\n- a friend
note cranewelcome Councillor Crane's welcome | TRANSCRIPT - the loop on band five hundred, typed out by the duty clerk because she was sick of hearing it.\n\n'This is Councillor Aldous Crane. If you can hear me, you have found Highwater, and Highwater has found you. You will have heard that the city sank. It did not. It will not, while I sit on the Council. Stop at the breakwater. Let the clerks weigh you. Every pound that comes into this city, I must answer for.'\n\n(In pencil, in the margin: He recorded it nine years ago. He says 'every pound' in exactly the same voice every time. I have started saying it along with him. If anyone hears me doing it, I will deny it. - N.)
note dobbs211 Complaint No. 211 | To the Harbor Council, Water Committee.\nCOMPLAINT No. 211\n\nSirs,\nThe boom squeaks. I reported the boom squeaking in Complaints 87, 140 and 198. It is the third post from the east. It squeaks on the ebb tide, in B-flat, and it can be heard at Pumpcrown, which is eleven miles away, which should not be possible, and yet.\n\nI am a pump foreman. I do not maintain booms. But I am the one who cannot sleep.\n\nI enclose a small tin of grease. Please give it to whoever maintains the boom. If nobody maintains the boom, please keep the tin, and think about that.\n\nYours, as ever, in hope,\nWilmer Dobbs, Foreman, Pumpcrown Works\n\n(Nailed to the post. The tin of grease is nailed up beside it.)
note radiodesk Radio desk | The customs radio desk: the receiver's plans in a drawer, a log of ships turned away.
note towerlocker Watch tower locker | The watch tower's locker: the aerial's plans, a coil of wire, a cold thermos.
loot radiodesk Blueprint_Reciever*1;CircuitBoard*1;Coconut*2
prop radiodesk loot.refill=0
loot towerlocker Blueprint_Antenna*1;CopperIngot*2;Rope*2
prop towerlocker loot.refill=0

prop customszone zone.id=customs_house
prop customszone zone.radius=3
prop customszone zone.message=The customs house. A radio desk, a board of rules, the sea at every window.

note keeperlog Keeper's log | LIGHTKEEPER'S LOG - the last page\n\nThey took the light off me in the spring. A customs house is cheaper than a lighthouse, Councillor Crane said, and shook my hand as if he was doing me a kindness. Thirty-one years I kept that lamp.\n\nNow the clerks wave boats in to be weighed, and wave the smugglers round the back for a fee. I watch from my porch. Their lamps go into the wreckers' cave on the west shore every new moon. I don't blame them. A filter costs a week's catch in the city. The boy two doors down went half blind from the brown water last summer.\n\nWhat the Authority catches goes into the bonded yard on the east side - walls in a maze, so nobody steals it back. Nell the night clerk knows the way through. Nell knows everything, and tells half.\n\n- Osric Pell, keeper (retired, against his will)
note wreckcavechest Wreckers' chest | The wreckers' chest: lamp oil, rope, and a dozen stamped permits with no names on them.
loot wreckcavechest Rope*3;Nail*8;Scrap*3;CopperIngot*1
prop wreckcavechest loot.refill=0
note seizedcrate Seized boat's hold | SEIZED BY THE HARBOR AUTHORITY - pending sale.\nThe hold: smuggled glass, plastic sheeting and a crate of nails the Authority forgot to sell.
loot seizedcrate Glass*3;Plastic*4;Nail*10
quest title=The Rumour Is True
quest intro=A city that never sank, the sailors say. Go into the customs house at the end of the breakwater.
step reach|customs_house|1|Go into the customs house at the end of the breakwater
step read|Authority entry rules|1|Read the Authority's entry rules
step read|Councillor Crane's welcome|1|Read the transcript of the Councillor's loop by the radio
step blueprint|Blueprint_Reciever|1|Take the receiver's plans from the radio desk
step blueprint|Blueprint_Antenna|1|Take the antenna's plans from the watch tower's locker
step collect|story:permit|1|Weigh your cargo and stamp a trader's permit
step read|Complaint No. 211|1|Read the complaint nailed to the boom post
step reach|signal_hill|1|Climb Signal Hill north of the breakwater
step read|Keeper's log|1|Read the lightkeeper's log in his ruined house on the east shore
step reach|wreckers_cave|1|Find the wreckers' cave in the west shore
step open|Seized boat's hold|1|Open the hold of the smugglers' boat the Authority seized
step read|Bonded yard notice|1|Read the notice at the gate of the bonded yard, on the east side
step reach|bw_heart|1|Find your way through the bonded yard's maze to its heart
step open|Seized goods strongbox|1|Open the seized-goods strongbox
step read|Clerk's last shift|1|Read the night clerk's last note
step read|A friend's tip|1|Read the folded note under the strongbox lid
quest done=The bazaar sells what the Authority says doesn't exist. Raft Row Bazaar - band 600.
quest reward=Coconut*3;Rope*2

save Breakwater Customs
